---
import Single from '../layouts/Single.astro';
import HomePhoto from '../components/HomePhoto.astro';
import ProfileLinks from '../components/ProfileLinks.astro';
import { formatDate } from '../i18n';

const lang = 'en';
---
<Single title="Parsa Kamalipour" lang={lang} twin="/fr/" description="About me" classes="home">
<section class="home-hero" aria-label="Introduction">
  <div class="home-hero__text">
    <div class="home-hero__id">
      <HomePhoto alt="Portrait of Parsa Kamalipour" />
      <p class="home-hero__role">MSc student in Computer Science<br>Algorithms &amp; Complexity Lab, Concordia University</p>
    </div>
    <p class="page__lead">Parsa studies community detection in social and complex networks: finding the groups hidden inside a graph, and judging whether they are real, with tools from algorithms and graph theory. He is a thesis-based master’s student at <a href="https://www.concordia.ca/ginacody/computer-science-software-eng.html">Concordia University</a> in Montréal, supervised by <a href="https://users.encs.concordia.ca/~haruty/">Professor Hovhannes Harutyunyan</a>.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="hero-btn hero-btn--primary" href="/files/ParsaKamalipour_CV.pdf"><i class="fas fa-download" aria-hidden="true"></i> Download CV</a>
      <a class="hero-btn hero-btn--ghost" href="/contact/"><i class="fas fa-envelope" aria-hidden="true"></i> Get in touch</a>
    </div>
    <ProfileLinks />
  </div>
  <figure class="hero-graph">
    <canvas role="img" aria-label="A random network of 56 nodes in four hidden groups. Label propagation colours each group as it finds it."></canvas>
    <figcaption>
      <span class="hero-graph__status" data-searching="Label propagation is looking for communities…" data-found="Label propagation found {n} communities in a random planted-partition graph." aria-live="polite">Label propagation is looking for communities…</span>
      <button type="button" class="hero-graph__again">New graph</button>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
<h2 class="section-heading section-heading--first" id="research">Research</h2>
<p>His thesis, <em><strong>Geodesic-Compact Community Detection and Quality Assessment in Social Networks</strong></em> (expected 2027), starts from a simple idea: the members of a good community are close to each other in shortest-path distance, compared with the rest of the network. This gives a way to find and judge communities without ground-truth labels. The work has so far produced <strong>Spider</strong>, a near-linear community detection algorithm that combines local and global steps (<em>Computers</em>, 2026), and a first-author study of the <strong>weighted-average Geodesic Distance Modularity (wGDM)</strong> with Metric Backbone sparsification as preprocessing for Leiden (<em>IEEE SNAMS 2025</em>, presented in Vienna). <a href="/biography/">Read the full biography</a></p>
<ul class="interest-tags" aria-label="Research interests">
  <li class="interest-tag">Graph theory</li>
  <li class="interest-tag">Algorithms</li>
  <li class="interest-tag">Complexity theory</li>
  <li class="interest-tag">Social network analysis</li>
  <li class="interest-tag">Community detection</li>
  <li class="interest-tag">Combinatorial optimization</li>
  <li class="interest-tag">Data mining</li>
</ul>
<dl class="stats-band" aria-label="Academic profile at a glance">
  <div class="stat-card"><dt class="stat-card__label">Publications</dt><dd class="stat-card__number">4</dd></div>
  <div class="stat-card"><dt class="stat-card__label">Courses as TA</dt><dd class="stat-card__number">15+</dd></div>
  <div class="stat-card"><dt class="stat-card__label">Teaching hours</dt><dd class="stat-card__number">1650+</dd></div>
  <div class="stat-card"><dt class="stat-card__label">Research positions</dt><dd class="stat-card__number">3</dd></div>
</dl>
<h2 class="section-heading" id="news">Recent news</h2>
<ol class="news-list">
  <li>
    <time datetime="2026-09">Sep 2026</time>
    <p>Graduate teaching assistant for four courses this fall: COEN 311, COEN 317, SOEN 363 and COMP 339.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <time datetime="2026-05">May 2026</time>
    <p>Received the <strong>Dean’s Excellence Award for Excellence in Teaching by a Teaching Assistant</strong> from the Gina Cody School of Engineering and Computer Science.</p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <time datetime="2026-02">Feb 2026</time>
    <p>“Spider Community Detection: Seeded Geodesic Expansion with Modularity-Guided Refinement and Greedy Merge Matching” is published in <em>Computers</em> 15(2), article 83. <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/computers15020083">Read the paper</a></p>
  </li>
  <li>
    <time datetime="2025-11">Nov 2025</time>
    <p>“From Dense Graphs to Meaningful Communities” presented at IEEE SNAMS 2025 in Vienna.</p>
  </li>
</ol>
<p class="news-list__more"><a href="/news/">All news</a></p>
<p class="page__updated">Last updated {formatDate(new Date(), lang)}</p>
</Single>
